1
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:26,000
The true story of a heist gone wrong... in all the right ways.

2
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:46,000
The Bank Job is a thriller, crime, drama film directed by Roger Donaldson.

3
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:06,000
Terry is a small-time car dealer trying to leave his
shady past behind and start a family.

4
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:26,000
Martine is a beautiful model from Terry's old
neighbourhood who knows that Terry is no angel.

5
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:46,000
When Martine proposes a foolproof plan to rob a bank, Terry recognises the
danger but realises this may be the opportunity of a lifetime.

6
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Terry Leather, played by Jason Statham.

7
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:26,000
Martine Love, played by Saffron Burrows.

8
00:42:40,000 --> 00:42:46,000
Kevin Swain, played by Stephen Campbell Moore.

9
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Dave Shilling, played by Daniel Mays.

10
00:53:20,000 --> 00:53:26,000
Guy Singer, played by James Faulkner.

11
00:58:40,000 --> 00:58:46,000
Quinn, played by Andrew Brooke.

12
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:06,000
The Bank Job is a 2008 heist thriller film directed by Roger
Donaldson and written by Dick Clement and Ian La Frenais.

13
01:09:20,000 --> 01:09:26,000
It is based on the 1971 burglary of Lloyds Bank
safety deposit boxes in Baker Street.

14
01:14:40,000 --> 01:14:46,000
It stars Jason Statham.

15
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
The producers allege that the story was prevented from being told in 1971 because of a
D-Notice, to protect a prominent member of the British royal family.

16
01:25:20,000 --> 01:25:26,000
According to the producers, this film is intended to reveal the truth for the first
time, although it apparently includes significant elements of fiction.

17
01:30:40,000 --> 01:30:46,000
The premiere was held in London on 18 February 2008, and it was released in
the UK on 29 February 2008 and in the US on 7 March 2008.

18
01:36:00,000 --> 01:36:06,000
It received mostly positive reviews from critics
and grossed $66 million worldwide.

19
01:41:20,000 --> 01:41:26,000
The film explores themes of london, england,
blackmail, 1970s, vault, car dealer.

20
01:46:40,000 --> 01:46:46,000
The tone is emotional and intense.
